{
  "_comment": [
    "HXEF v1 test vectors (spec 048, docs/formats/encrypted-folder-v1.md).",
    "The expected outcome of one head case was changed by hand afterwards (a recipient whose key id the reader holds but which does not unwrap is damaged); its bytes are unchanged.",
    "Generated once by a throwaway Python script written from the format document only, not from",
    "holzi's implementation: XChaCha20-Poly1305 from PyNaCl 1.6.2 (libsodium,",
    "crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_encrypt), HKDF-SHA256 from Python's hmac and hashlib.",
    "Fixed inputs are literal byte ranges or the first n bytes of SHA-256 over a label such as",
    "'dek/one'. Plaintext of a content object of size s: byte i = i mod 251.",
    "Binary values are lowercase hex; ids also as lowercase unpadded Base32 where the format names them.",
    "Large content objects carry object_len and object_sha256 instead of the bytes: a reader seals",
    "the plaintext with the given dek, cid and nonce_prefix, which must give exactly that hash.",
    "Content cases apply ops in order to the named object: flip = XOR 0x01 at an offset,",
    "truncate = keep the first n bytes, append = add hex bytes, swap = [a, b, len] exchanges two",
    "ranges, replace = [offset, hex] overwrites. Every content, sidecar and failing dek case must be refused."
  ],
